          ],
          "issue": "I'm pausing before I start the workflow. Item B needs a wording choice from you, and the two options aren't equivalent. Option 2 says the app is opening the mail app, which implies behavior `useCopyEmail` would have to provide. Option 1 only tells the visitor the address. I haven't written any files, and I haven't started the planner, checker, executor or verifier.\n\nOnce you choose, I'll run the full validate workflow with that wording. It will add `copyFallback(address)` to `src/lib/copy.ts` and the `copyFallback names the address` test to `tests/unit/copy.test.ts`. `COPY_FALLBACK` stays exported and unchanged.\n\nWhich wording should `copyFallback` return?\n1. `Couldn’t copy. Email me at <address>.`\n2. `Couldn’t copy the address. Opening your mail app to <address>.`",
          "recommendation": null,
          "options": [
            {
              "key": "1",
              "kind": "choice",
              "label": "`Couldn’t copy. Email me at <address>.`"
            },
            {
              "key": "2",
              "kind": "choice",
              "label": "`Couldn’t copy the address. Opening your mail app to <address>.`"
            }
          ],
          "consequences": {
            "1": "item B resumes with this answer",
            "2": "item B resumes with this answer"
          },
